      },
      "text": "We analyze the LCT attack on a noised pseudorandom sequence generator involving a primitive known as The Binary Rate Multiplier (BRM). BRM consists of 2 linear feedback shift registers (LFSRs). One of them, the clocking LFSR (LFSRs), determines the clocking sequence for the clocked LFSR (LFSRu), see Fig. 1.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
